From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:39:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 045/191] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the Fast mode
 switch

The dual review of the Fast mode switch (2026-10-14: Codex one finding,
Claude's /code-review nine, Reid had all real ones fixed) found several ways
fast mode could end up on, billing usage credits, while the switch showed it
off.

- Turning fast mode on now requires "fastModePerSessionOptIn": true in the
  host's Claude settings (409 claude_native_fast_mode_needs_per_session
  otherwise); turning it off never does. GET reports per_session, and the
  switch says "Needs per-session fast mode on this host".
- Once /fast is typed the runner never answers a failure: mid-turn (Claude
  Code applies it when the reply finishes) or unconfirmed after 10 seconds it
  answers 202 pending with the reason, and the web holds the requested state,
  re-reads every 2 seconds while the menu is open and again on the next open.
- The server waits 75 seconds for the runner, longer than its worst case, and
  treats no answer as pending instead of "no live runner".
- A per-session lock covers the whole check, type and confirm sequence, and
  the "already there" shortcut is gone, so two quick flips cannot report a
  state the terminal is not in.
- Off stays allowed on a model without fast mode.
- While a flip is pending the model and effort picks are disabled, so /model
  cannot be typed right behind /fast.
- A flip never starts a Claude Code terminal: with no live pane it answers 409
  claude_native_no_terminal.
- A successful read clears an old error, the context.json name comes from the
  status writer, and comments in upstream files describe the code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
